# Rust
# Slashless, deliberately -- a trailing slash matches a DIRECTORY ONLY, so a
# symlink of the same name slips past it (that is exactly how a machine-specific
# node_modules link got committed; see the Node section below).
target
# Cross-compile and per-lane target dirs. `target` alone does NOT cover these --
# it is a different NAME, not a subdirectory. `cargo check --target
# x86_64-pc-windows-gnu` wrote target-win/, which was therefore never ignored,
# and the public-release audit then scanned 849 build artifacts full of an
# absolute /home/... path and failed. Build output is never publishable.
target-*
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Tauri
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/
apps/osl-hub/binaries/

# Node
# No trailing slash, deliberately. `node_modules/` matches a DIRECTORY only, so
# a SYMLINK named node_modules is not ignored by it -- which is how
# apps/osl-hub-ui/node_modules came to be committed as a tracked mode-120000
# link to an absolute path outside the repo (910a79335, removed in 2e4d8598d).
# A machine-specific absolute path in the index breaks
# every other checkout: `npm ci` deletes the link, and a run where it resolved
# to nothing made four binding ledgers fail with
# "Cannot find module 'vite/package.json'". The slashless form ignores the
# directory AND the symlink, so `git add -A` cannot re-commit it.
node_modules
dist/
build/
.parcel-cache/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Editor
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local config / secrets
.env
.env.local
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
KEYVAULT.md
.claude/settings.local.json
.serena/
graphify-out/
*.log
apps/osl-hub-ui/screenshots/*.png
evidence/task-3532-resize-redraw/

# Build outputs
*.msi
*.exe
*.dmg

# Keyserver runtime artifacts
keyserver/keyserver.db
keyserver/keyserver.db-wal
keyserver/keyserver.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite-wal
*.sqlite-shm

# Reference clones for Layer 10 / 11 (Discord webpack research).
# Vendored read-only via git clone — not part of the build.
reference/
.wrangler/

# Local dispatch signals -- NEVER commit these. Agents committed .task-blocked
# to their branches and every one of ~190 task branches then conflicted on it,
# stalling the entire harvest.
.task-blocked
.task-already-done
